; The whole compiler, end to end, on a bundle whose golden output pins down
; how functions passed as arguments are compiled, spec sections 5.7 and
; 10.2.
;
; Like bundle_prelude this supplies no main of its own and takes the
; compiler's. In the input, the prelude and the program each define key,
; and the program passes its own to the prelude's apply_twice, directly and
; through via, which passes its parameter on. So the copies are named
; .Fkey, a call through f in a prelude copy is a direct call of the
; program's @l0_f_key and never the prelude's, the tail call through f is
; musttail, and via's tail call of its copy of apply_twice is too. pick is
; given a def with a type parameter, idt, at int, which its copy names
; .Pidt.0. A function with function parameters has no code of its own.
